/// A module-suffix scope naming a module this file cannot reach is E0240, not
/// a silent bind to it.
///
/// `Alpha::Text` is compiled (see registry.cryo) but never imported here, so
/// `Text` binds to nothing in scope. The resolver used to scan the module
/// graph for any namespace ending in `::Text` and bind to whatever it found -
/// which is how a call reached a module its file never imported.
namespace ResolutionUnreachableModule::Main;

import ResolutionUnreachableModule::Registry;
import ResolutionUnreachableModule::Solo::Only;

/// The control: one module ends in `::Only` and this file imports it, so the
/// same suffix machinery must still answer.  A gate that rejects this has
/// stopped resolving module-suffix scopes rather than resolving them against
/// the imports.
///
/// It lives in its own function, several lines from the rejection below,
/// because the renderer echoes the source around an error - a control sharing
/// that line would appear in the output no matter what the compiler decided
/// about it, and could not be asserted absent.
function control() -> i32 {
    return Only::ping();
}

function main(argc: int, argv: string*) -> int {
    return (Text::tag() + control()) as int;
}
